reviews.text:
I don't doubt that the doctors are well-trained and competent, but unfortunately, I noticed that this clinic lacks a CRUCIAL quality for a veterinarian: empathy. Not even a caress for the dog, who was already very agitated; mistaking him twice for a female, despite having told them he was a male;
even the way they spoke to the dog's owner showed no reassurance or empathy, just detachment and coldness. I also asked for the reports that same evening, but nothing. I called back the next day, asking again since it was very urgent given that the dog was in critical condition, but they told me to wait a little longer.
Kind regards
